        "original_id": "602795d0-82bd-5120-ada8-f501dc98009d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Marvin Gaye, Marvin Gay Sr., Alberta, Frankie, Zeola, Gordon Banks, Marvin III, Anna, Denise Gordy, Nona\n- Organizations: House of God\n- Places: Los Angeles\n\nFacts:\n- Marvin Pentz Gay Sr. was born on October 1, 1914, and died on October 10, 1998.\n- Marvin Gay Sr. was an American minister of the House of God.\n- Marvin Gay Sr. was the father of American recording artist Marvin Gaye.\n- Marvin Gaye's notable relatives included his father Marvin Gay Sr., his mother Alberta, his brother Frankie, his sister Zeola, his brother-in-law Gordon Banks, his son Marvin III, and his daughter Nona.\n- Marvin III was adopted by Marvin Gaye's first wife Anna from her niece Denise Gordy.\n- On April 1, 1984, Marvin Gay Sr. shot and killed Marvin Gaye after an argument at their home in Los Angeles.",
